Bank of Canada rate decision on October 28 could shift mortgage costs and TFSA dividend strategies for Canadian investors. This is Modern Investing Techniques, episode 210. After the policy picture, we work evaluation screen, a simulated coinbase weekly hold, and how a market order actually fills when the book thins, plus the trade review and tools. Quick reminder, everything we discuss here is for education and entertainment. The practice investment of the day uses simulated trades

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:34.360
with no real money. I'm not a licensed financial advisor, and this isn't financial advice.

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:39.992
Always do your own research before putting real money to work. The Bank of Canada will publish

00:00:39.992 --> 00:00:45.892
updated economic forecasts with its monetary policy report, and the Federal Reserve Path is the other

00:00:45.892 --> 00:00:55.412
half of that same rate frame. The S&amp;P 500 closed at 7,624, down 0.5%, and the Toronto Stock Exchange

00:00:55.412 --> 00:01:06.232
Composite, or TSX, declines 0.5% to 35,788. The NASDAQ Composite finished at 25,955,

00:01:06.272 --> 00:01:14.492
off 0.2% up 11.70% year-to-date, and up 16.01% since the practice portfolio opened

00:01:14.492 --> 00:01:21.072
on March 16, 2026. Inflation prints and corporate earnings are shaping sentiment this week, with

00:01:21.072 --> 00:01:23.972
