00:01:24.866 --> 00:01:30.046
About 14 days ago, we picked BB on a valuation screen after revenue guidance was raised,

00:01:30.646 --> 00:01:33.426
and it closed down 3.59%.

00:01:33.426 --> 00:01:37.706
Valuation screening looks for stocks trading at depressed multiples relative to earnings

00:01:37.706 --> 00:01:42.166
or book value, and that buffer matters when momentum rotates out of growth names.

00:01:42.746 --> 00:01:48.046
Broughter indices pulled back in this tape, while select Canadian names still show revenue visibility,

00:01:48.546 --> 00:01:50.146
which is when this screen earns a look.

00:01:50.146 --> 00:01:56.366
you can run it on free tools at WealthSimple or Questrade by filtering TSX listed financials,

00:01:56.546 --> 00:01:59.006
or real estate investment trusts, or REITs.

00:01:59.286 --> 00:02:04.466
For a forward price to earnings multiple, or PE, below the sector average, then you

00:02:04.466 --> 00:02:09.166
confirm free cash flow yield above 5% before the name even reaches a watch list.

00:02:09.666 --> 00:02:14.626
Coinbase and PayPal are two major players in the future of finance, but their business models

00:02:14.626 --> 00:02:19.726
and valuations sit far apart, and that gap is a relative value choice rather than a single

00:02:19.726 --> 00:02:25.146
name bet. The Motley Fools comparative read is that Coinbase's distinct model versus PayPal

00:02:25.146 --> 00:02:31.166
leaves room for multiple expansion if crypto volume stabilized. This approach performed best in

00:02:31.166 --> 00:02:37.326
the 2022 and 2023 rate hike cycles when multiple compression created entry points that later

00:02:37.326 --> 00:02:43.546
re-rated on stable earnings. The risk is a value trap where a cheap multiple reflects structural decline

00:02:43.546 --> 00:02:49.386
rather than temporary mispricing. Pair every hit with a same day volume check so you are not buying

00:02:49.386 --> 00:02:54.366
a quiet name that only looks cheap on the spreadsheet. I have no financial relationship

00:02:54.366 --> 00:02:58.806
with wealth, simple or quest trade. They are simply where a Canadian account can run that

00:02:58.806 --> 00:03:05.635
screen without extra cost. Coinbase Global, ticker COIN on the NASDAQ, is this week simulated

00:03:05.635 --> 00:03:11.295
weekly hold, a tech sector FinTech name, and this is a simulated trade for learning purposes

00:03:11.295 --> 00:03:16.415
with no real money involved. The strategy is a valuation entry on a name trading at a

00:03:16.415 --> 00:03:21.355
discount to growth peers, while sector rotation into Fintech is the setup we are testing.

00:03:22.035 --> 00:03:27.355
Confidence is medium, the valuation discount, and the sector setup align, yet broader market

00:03:27.355 --> 00:03:31.015
volatility from geopolitical headlines is still an uncertainty factor.

00:03:31.675 --> 00:03:36.635
Price action relative to recent moving averages suggests room for a rebound if volume confirms

00:03:36.635 --> 00:03:37.915
above average levels.

00:03:38.495 --> 00:03:43.595
In validation is a break below the 50-day moving average on volume above the 20-day average,

00:03:43.595 --> 00:03:49.885
and that line is the habit to copy before any size goes on. Maximum acceptable loss is

00:03:49.885 --> 00:03:55.745
caped at 8% through that moving average invalidation, so a $1,000 position limits dollar

00:03:55.745 --> 00:04:02.645
risk to $80. The five-session target is plus 3% to plus 6% if rotation into FinTech names

00:04:02.645 --> 00:04:08.665
continues, with entry at the next open under the published rules. An earlier catalyst hold

00:04:08.665 --> 00:04:13.865
taught us to cross-check sector rotation signals before we size an entry, and that is why this

00:04:13.865 --> 00:04:18.485
Coinbase ticket stays at medium confidence until the rotation actually prints in the tape.

00:04:19.065 --> 00:04:23.225
We will track the simulated shares across five sessions and judge the result against

00:04:23.225 --> 00:04:27.665
the NASDAQ over that same window, not against the story we liked on the way in.

00:04:28.285 --> 00:04:31.425
EDV was an earlier weekly hold, not the latest close.

00:04:32.025 --> 00:04:37.265
A catalyst play on scheduled third quarter 2026 results that could reset production and cost

00:04:37.265 --> 00:04:37.665
guidance.

00:04:37.665 --> 00:04:43.905
We simulated buying at the Wednesday open at $76 Canadian and exiting at the Tuesday

00:04:43.905 --> 00:04:50.225
close at $77 Canadian in $18. A six calendar day window from Wednesday to Tuesday.

00:04:50.645 --> 00:04:59.525
The simulated $1,000 position gained 1.55%, or $15.53. Over that same window, the NASDAQ

00:04:59.525 --> 00:05:07.345
moved down 0.10%, so the trade booked plus 1.65% of Alpha. The catalyst produced a modest

00:05:07.345 --> 00:05:13.665
gain, yet single-name exposure still lagged broader rotation. Rule, always cross-check sector

00:05:13.665 --> 00:05:18.925
rotation signals before sizing earnings-driven entries. That rotation check is the analytical

00:05:18.925 --> 00:05:24.405
technique this whole tested, and it is why today's Coinbase size stays modest instead of being

00:05:24.405 --> 00:05:31.090
treated as a high confidence earnings bet. Unusual whales surfaces unusual options trades and dark

