00:08:45.455 --> 00:08:52.595
87 total simulated trades at a 52% win rate, 45 wins produced a cumulative P&amp;L of minus

00:08:52.595 --> 00:08:59.295
$14.73, and that full history stays on the page as history, not as the method test.

00:08:59.815 --> 00:09:04.315
The process is adjusting around sector rotation confirmation on valuation entries,

00:09:04.755 --> 00:09:09.942
because that is the pattern the recent holds keep sending back. You placed a market order for

00:09:09.942 --> 00:09:15.262
200 shares of a TSX listed name at the open on a day when producer price data was moving

00:09:15.262 --> 00:09:21.722
energy-exposed names. The raw materials price index jumped 4.8% in September, powered

00:09:21.722 --> 00:09:27.642
by a 14.4% surge in crude energy products, and that is the tape in which algorithms start

00:09:27.642 --> 00:09:32.582
yanking bids. The mechanism that actually determined your fill was limit-order book depth,

00:09:33.102 --> 00:09:38.362
which thinned quickly as those bids disappeared, and the execution came in 12 cents worse than

00:09:38.362 --> 00:09:43.642
the displayed quote. Professional desks counter that by routing through an electronic communication

00:09:43.642 --> 00:09:49.402
network, or ECN, or by using a midpoint peg that splits the spread rather than crossing it

00:09:49.402 --> 00:09:55.862
immediately. Producer prices rose 2.0% over the month, flagging a stronger pipeline of costs

00:09:55.862 --> 00:10:01.902
into future inflation gauges, and higher input prices often feed borrowing costs as rate expectations

00:10:01.902 --> 00:10:07.742
adjust. That squeeze hits manufacturer margins if they cannot pass on energy and materials costs,

00:10:07.742 --> 00:10:14.322
and new home prices slipped 0.2%, adding pressure and cost sensitive sectors where slippage compounds.

00:10:15.042 --> 00:10:20.782
Preview the order book depth and switch to a limit order when the spread exceeds 0.3% of the last trade.

00:10:21.342 --> 00:10:27.722
The misconception to drop is that your broker's best execution guarantee always delivers the mid price on low volume names.

00:10:28.302 --> 00:10:28.862
It does not.

